From 13fa018884d0745b3577d135f1ab7f2177299020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PJ Onori <pj.onori@sanity.io>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:18:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: full MCP surface parity for the CLI; MCP server
 becomes a thin wrapper
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An MCP server advertises four capability groups: instructions, tools,
prompts, and resources. Only tools were shared (registry.js); the other
three were defined inside server.js, so no CLI command could reach them
and the MCP server could not be reduced to a transport.

Extract all four into one shared core:

- src/surface.js — createSurface() returns toolDefs/dispatch,
  listPrompts/getPrompt, listResources/readResource, getInstructions.
- src/prompts.js — the prompt catalog and renderer.
- src/instructions.js — the agent instruction block.
- src/intro.js — intro-entity rendering, used by both of the above.

server.js drops 363 -> ~100 lines and now defines nothing: protocol
handlers delegating to the surface. No protocol-visible behavior change.

CLI gains a command per capability group:

- dsds prompt [<name>] [--task <text>]
- dsds resource [<uri|identifier>]
- dsds instructions

doctor gains an "mcp surface" check that reports what the surface
resolves to and reads every resource, so one that fails to serialize is a
failing check rather than a surprise at call time. The manifest gains
capabilities, prompts, and resources. Parity tests widen from tools to
all four groups.

Fix, found by dsds resource against the 199-entity Sanity UI document:
resources/read threw "Converting circular structure to JSON" on every
entity in a document with a shared[] pool. The loader annotates entities
with __sharedEntries, whose members carry the same pool, making a loaded
0.20.0 entity cyclic. The reader now drops the loader's internal __ keys,
which terminates and leaves the body as the authored document. Confirmed
over the real protocol: MCP error -32603 before, a clean read after.

dsds-mcp 0.4.0, dsds-cli 0.2.0. 366 + 116 tests green.

